A||N||2||helomech||HT 3.4 liter GM crate engine||||5||
Z||000000||helomech||01-13-2001||10:17 PM||||Does anyone know if the General motors HT 3.4 liter engine &lt;http://www.gmgoodwrench.com/crate_engine/global/ix_ht34.htm&gt; is compatible with the 2.8 Liter parts in the fiero? The GM page talks about the S-10/S-15 2.8 liter components bolting right up but there is no mention of other GM engines. Is the Chev/GMC 2.8 the same block as the Pontiac 2.8? I've got an 85 GT that I am going to do a Fino or a Finale rebody, and I'm looking at engine options.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-13-2001||10:24 PM||||This is the same engine used in the '93-'95 Camaro/Firebird.  It is identicl to the Fiero 2.8, meaning that your 2.8 accessories will bolt on to it (intake, etc.).<P>You may consider buying a low mileage Camaro/Firebird 3.4 and go that route instead.......the crate motor doesn't come with injectors.<P>Whichever route you go you must redrill the starter holes.  The starter on the 3.4 is on the wrong side for the Fiero (it interferes with the axles).<P>Good luck......this is the most popular (and easiest overall) engine swap there is for the Fiero.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||01-13-2001||10:45 PM||||The 3.4 topic has been covered in great detail on several (possible hundreds) posts. Use the search function at the top right- make sure you search the Tech Discussion portion and you should find hours of reading material.||||reg||1
